      <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="fixupTemplateInstantiations_8h_1ad2238f56b9824f5cbca2cc332d0d6bd3" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void fixupTemplateInstantiations</definition>
        <argsstring>(SgNode *node)</argsstring>
        <name>fixupTemplateInstantiations</name>
        <param>
          <type>SgNode *</type>
          <declname>node</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Fixups template specializations generated by ROSE from template instantiations. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Template instantions generated in either the prelink phase or as part of the initial compilation should be marked as comiler generated since they have no source position.</para><para>We have to output the declaration of the specialization after the template declaration and before it&apos;s first use in the source file. It is an error to transform the specialization in a file where it is not first used (e.g. if the first use appears in a header file then the first use could appear before the declaration). Note also that only those template specializations that are transformed are output by ROSE. </para>        </detaileddescription>
